# vss — Vintage Story modding reference

A lookup skill over the **local game-understanding base** built by `vss-codex`. It tells you *where to
look* and *how to read it* — it never edits anything. Paths are relative to the workspace root (the
folder that contains the `vss-codex` and `vs-game-reference` directories).

> Built from VS **{{VS_VERSION}}** ({{GENERATED_ON}}) by `vss-codex` — {{API_TYPES}} API types in
> {{API_NAMESPACES}} namespaces ({{COVERAGE_PCT}}% documented), {{EVENTS}} events, {{ENUMS}} enums,
> {{LIB_TYPES}} engine types. Rebuild with `vss-codex/vss-codex.ps1` after a VS update.

> **Local & gitignored.** The `vs-game-reference/` tree (decompiled VS binaries + generated docs) is
> derived from proprietary game binaries — it is gitignored and must **never** be committed or shared.
> It is pinned to the VS build it was generated from — re-run `vss-codex/vss-codex.ps1` after a VS
> update (see `vs-game-reference/README.md`).

## Where everything lives

| What | Path |
|---|---|
| **Hand notes** (read first) | `vs-game-reference/docs/README.md`, `docs/entity-simulation.md` |
| **API endpoints** (public surface + official + inherited summaries, ctors, `[Obsolete]`) | `vs-game-reference/docs/generated/api/INDEX.md` → one file per namespace |
| **Events & delegates** (consolidated) | `vs-game-reference/docs/generated/api/events.md` |
| **Enums index** | `vs-game-reference/docs/generated/api/enums.md` |
| **Engine internals** (`VintagestoryLib` public types: ServerMain, PhysicsManager…) | `vs-game-reference/docs/generated/api/lib/INDEX.md` |
| **Harmony catalog** (every method ✓/✗ patchable) | `vs-game-reference/docs/generated/harmony/INDEX.md` → `patchable-<assembly>.md` |
| **Harmony hotspots** (curated, server-perf) | `vs-game-reference/docs/generated/harmony/high-value-targets.md` |
| **Version diff** (after a VS update) | `vs-game-reference/docs/generated/CHANGELOG-<old>-to-<new>.md` |
| **Raw decompiled source** (ground truth) | `vs-game-reference/decompiled/<assembly>/<namespace-as-folders>/<Type>.cs` |
| **Skill how-tos** | `references/` (this skill) |
| **Code examples** | `examples/` (this skill) |

## Routing — pick the cheapest source that answers the question

1. **"What does API X do / what's its signature?"** → Grep `docs/generated/api/` (official +
   inherited summaries). Don't read the whole namespace file — Grep the type name.
2. **"What event do I subscribe to?" / "what are the values of enum Z?"** → `api/events.md` /
   `api/enums.md` (consolidated; faster than hunting per-type).
3. **"How does the engine actually do Y (tick, spawn, save, light)?"** → start with the hand notes
   (`docs/entity-simulation.md`); for the engine type surface use `api/lib/`, then the raw source
   under `decompiled/VintagestoryLib/Vintagestory.Server/`.
4. **"Can I Harmony-patch method Z?"** → Grep the relevant `patchable-<assembly>.md` for the ✓/✗ flag.
5. **"Where should I patch for performance?"** → `high-value-targets.md` first.
6. **"How do I use the API / write a patch?"** → `references/api-usage.md`, `references/harmony-usage.md`,
   and the `examples/`.
7. **Need exact behavior / line numbers?** → open the decompiled `.cs`. It is the source of truth;
   the generated docs are an index over it.

See `references/search-strategy.md` for concrete Grep/Glob recipes.

## Hard rules

- **Never edit** under `vs-game-reference/` by hand except the curated `high-value-targets.md`.
  `INDEX.md` / `patchable-*.md` / `api/*` are regenerated by `vss-codex.ps1`.
- **Prefer the public API over a Harmony patch** whenever the engine exposes the knob — patches are
  version-fragile. (Example: keep chunks loaded with the native `WorldManager.LoadChunkColumn` call,
  or force entity activity via the public `AlwaysActive` property, instead of patching.)
- Cite sources as `assembly/path:line` so they're clickable.

